---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Recovery Diagnostics"
  description="Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recovery readiness, database recovery status, corruption, archive gaps and recovery area pressure."
>
  <main>
    <section class="resource-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
        <h1>Recovery <span class="hero-accent">Diagnostics</span></h1>
        <p>
          Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recovery readiness, database recovery
          status, corruption, archive gaps and recovery area pressure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Check recovery readiness from multiple angles</h2>
          <p>
            Recovery diagnostics should combine database state, files requiring
            recovery, corruption checks, archived redo gaps, recovery area usage
            and recent RMAN activity. These queries provide a practical starting
            point for reviewing recovery readiness.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">01 · DATABASE STATUS</p>
              <h2>Review database recovery state</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review the database role, open mode, logging mode and flashback
              status as the first recovery-readiness check.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    name,
    db_unique_name,
    database_role,
    open_mode,
    log_mode,
    flashback_on
FROM v$database;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">02 · RECOVERY FILES</p>
              <h2>Find files requiring recovery</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Identify data files currently reported as requiring media recovery
              and review the associated recovery change and time.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    file#,
    error,
    online_status,
    change#,
    time
FROM v$recover_file
ORDER BY file#;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">03 · CORRUPTION</p>
              <h2>Check reported block corruption</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review blocks reported as corrupt by Oracle to identify files and
              block ranges that may require further investigation or recovery.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    file#,
    block#,
    blocks,
    corruption_change#,
    corruption_type
FROM v$database_block_corruption
ORDER BY file#, block#;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">04 · ARCHIVE GAPS</p>
              <h2>Check for archived redo gaps</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review archive gaps reported by Oracle, which can be important when
              validating redo availability for recovery or standby operations.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    thread#,
    low_sequence#,
    high_sequence#
FROM v$archive_gap
ORDER BY thread#;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">05 · RECOVERY AREA</p>
              <h2>Review recovery area pressure</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Check recovery area capacity, current usage and reclaimable space
              to identify storage pressure that can affect recovery operations.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    name,
    space_limit / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS limit_gb,
    space_used / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS used_gb,
    space_reclaimable / 1024 / 1024 / 1024 AS reclaimable_gb,
    number_of_files
FROM v$recovery_file_dest;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <p class="resource-block__label">06 · RMAN ACTIVITY</p>
              <h2>Review recent RMAN operations</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review recent RMAN operations, their status and execution time to
              identify backup or recovery activity that needs attention.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    operation,
    status,
    start_time,
    end_time,
    ROUND(
        (end_time - start_time) * 24 * 60,
        1
    ) AS duration_minutes
FROM v$rman_status
WHERE start_time &gt;= SYSDATE - 7
ORDER BY start_time DESC;</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX · BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Recovery diagnostics should connect evidence.</h2>
          <p>
            Database state, files requiring recovery, corruption, archive gaps,
            recovery area usage and RMAN activity each show a different part of
            the recovery picture. Reviewing them together provides better
            operational context than relying on a single status check.
          </p>
          <p>
            Use these queries as an investigation starting point and correlate
            the results with the recovery procedure, backup strategy and
            environment-specific configuration.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/backup-recovery/">
            Back to Backup &amp; Recovery
          </a>
          <a class="resource-actions__link" href="/tools/backup-recovery/backup-space/">
            Read Backup Space
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.resource-hero {
  padding-top: 72px;
  padding-bottom: 72px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
}
.resource-hero h1 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px);
  line-height: 1.05;
  letter-spacing: -0.04em;
}
.resource-hero .hero-accent {
  color: var(--orange);
}
.resource-hero > .container > p:last-child {
  max-width: 900px;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}
.resource-section {
  padding-top: 56px;
  padding-bottom: 72px;
}
.resource-intro {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}
.resource-intro .eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.resource-intro h2 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.15;
}
.resource-intro p:not(.eyebrow) {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}
.resource-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 22px;
  align-items: start;
}
.resource-block {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  min-width: 0;
  height: 560px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow: hidden;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 30px;
  background: #ffffff;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  transition:
    border-color 0.22s ease,
    box-shadow 0.22s ease,
    transform 0.22s ease;
}
.resource-block:hover {
  border-color: #d8dce1;
  box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
  transform: translateY(-3px);
}
.resource-block__header {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.resource-block__label {
  margin-bottom: 9px;
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.2;
}
.resource-block h2 {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}
.resource-block__description {
  min-height: 48px;
  margin: 0 0 22px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}
.resource-block pre {
  position: relative;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-height: 0;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 22px;
  overflow-x: auto;
  overflow-y: auto;
  white-space: pre;
  background: #2f353d;
  border-radius: 10px;
  color: #f3f4f6;
  font-family:
    "Cascadia Code",
    "Consolas",
    "Courier New",
    monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.7;
}
.resource-block code {
  font-family: inherit;
  white-space: pre;
}
.resource-copy-button {
  position: absolute;
  top: 10px;
  right: 10px;
  padding: 5px 9px;
  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #374151;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  cursor: pointer;
  z-index: 2;
}
.resource-copy-button:hover {
  background: #f3f4f6;
}
.resource-note {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-top: 56px;
  padding: 30px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  background: #f7f8fa;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.75;
}
.resource-note .eyebrow {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.resource-note h2 {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.15;
}
.resource-note p:not(.eyebrow) {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.resource-note p:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}
.resource-note code {
  padding: 1px 4px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  background: #eef0f2;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family:
    "Cascadia Code",
    "Consolas",
    "Courier New",
    monospace;
  font-size: 0.92em;
}
.resource-actions {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 24px;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  margin-top: 32px;
}
.resource-actions__link {
  color: var(--orange);
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-decoration: none;
}
.resource-actions__link:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}
@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
@media (max-width: 680px) {
  .resource-hero {
    padding-top: 58px;
    padding-bottom: 54px;
  }
  .resource-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 12vw, 54px);
  }
  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 42px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }
  .resource-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .resource-block {
    height: 520px;
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 0;
  }
  .resource-block pre {
    padding: 18px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .resource-note {
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .resource-actions {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px;
  }
}
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";
    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>
